dialogue desert_recruit_support
title: Stranded in the red
trigger: ThemeStart desert
speaker commander $commander
speaker recruit $recruit
speaker backer $party:2

node meet recruit
  Hey! White wagon! Don't run me down, I'm not with the Choir. I just look this dusty.
  -> reply

node reply commander
  You're a long way from the Underspire. What are you doing out in the red?
  * Climb aboard. Explain on the way. -> aboard
  * It's rough out here. -> warned
  * Who left you out here? -> stiffed

node aboard recruit
  Not so fast. I don't climb into anything I haven't looked under first.
  -> inspect

node warned recruit
  Rough? The Choir's dig hired me to fix their walkers, then stiffed me. They're cracking the Manalith's fallen shell open out there.
  -> inspect

node stiffed recruit
  The Choir's dig. Hired me to keep their walkers walking, paid me in blessings, and left me a canteen and a direction.
  -> inspect

node inspect recruit
  Your axle's cracked, by the way. And there's an orb bolted under the bench that's humming. Those don't hum. Nothing from Halcyon hums anymore.
  -> orb

node orb commander
  The Engineer is already halfway under the wagon.
  * It does that near me. -> near
  * Can you fix the axle? -> axle

node near recruit
  Near you. Step back. Further. It's gone quiet. Come closer. It's humming again. That's not possible, and I'd like to take it apart.
  -> backer

node axle recruit
  Of course I can fix the axle. The question is whether you can pay better than the Choir did.
  -> pay

node pay commander
  The Engineer waits, wrench in hand.
  * Water, and a ride out of the red. -> fair
  * Nothing yet. But we won't leave you stranded. -> promise

node fair recruit
  Water is the only coin out here that nobody fakes. Done.
  -> backer

node promise recruit
  Everyone says that. The Choir said it. Still, you stopped the wagon, which is more than they did.
  -> backer

node backer backer
  It's not only the bench orb. In a fight our orbs wake around the Commander. Every one of them.
  -> believe

node believe recruit
  Every orb in a fight? The dig would kill for that. They're breaking open a fallen shell for a fraction of it.
  -> stakes

node stakes commander
  The Commander looks out over the red, toward the dig.
  * Then come keep it out of their hands. -> joined
  * The Ember will want it too. -> ember

node ember recruit
  The Ember? Then you're driving the whitest wagon in the red past the people who burn white things. You'll need it to run faster than it does.
  -> joined

node joined recruit
  Deal. I'll fix your axle on the move. And keep the wagon moving. The Ember hates anything white.
  do: JoinHero engineer role=Support
  * Welcome aboard, Engineer. -> welcome
    do: AddTrust $recruit 10
  * Thank the one who vouched for us. -> credit
    do: AddTrust $recruit 5
    do: AddCohesion $recruit $party:2 10
  * Fix the axle first. The orb can wait. -> terms
    do: AddTrust $recruit -5
    do: AddCohesion $recruit $party:2 5

node welcome recruit
  Aboard and under it. Wake me if anything else starts humming.

node credit backer
  I only said what I saw. You'd have climbed under the wagon either way.
  -> thanks

node thanks recruit
  Probably. But it's nice to be asked for once, instead of hired.

node terms recruit
  Fine. Axle first. But I'm keeping a list of questions, and it's getting long.
